# Fanne Linux desktop
# NOTE: xfce4-goodies is intentionally NOT installed here — it's a large
# grab-bag metapackage. A curated slice of it is offered as an opt-in extra
# through Calamares (see config/includes.chroot/etc/calamares/modules/
# packagechooser.conf) instead of shipping unconditionally on the live image.
task-xfce-desktop
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter

# Init system: sysvinit instead of systemd, plus the session-tracking and
# udev/logind replacements that NetworkManager, PipeWire, XFCE, and Calamares
# need in place of systemd-logind.
sysvinit-core
live-config-sysvinit
elogind
libpam-elogind

# Live environment and graphical installer
live-boot
live-config
# Pulled in for free by tasksel/task-desktop on Debian, but not by
# task-xfce-desktop on Devuan Ceres. live-config's 0030-user-setup
# component requires this package to actually create the live user;
# without it, it silently exits early (pkg_is_installed check fails)
# and sudo/LightDM autologin break for lack of a 'user' account.
user-setup
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
plymouth
plymouth-themes

# Hardware, networking, and audio
network-manager
network-manager-applet
nm-connection-editor
pipewire
pipewire-audio
wireplumber
pavucontrol
# fwupd intentionally NOT installed: current fwupd versions depend on real
# libsystemd0 (bus/device APIs elogind-compat doesn't provide), which
# conflicts with libpam-elogind/libelogind-compat on Devuan Ceres. Revisit
# once Devuan's elogind-compat catches up, or offer it as an opt-in extra.
firmware-linux-free
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek

# Virtual machine guest integration. Each of these only activates itself
# when it detects its matching hypervisor (DMI/PCI probing at boot), so
# they're harmless no-ops on real hardware and on the "wrong" hypervisor.
# Shipping all three unconditionally is what lets one image behave well
# in VirtualBox, VMware, and QEMU/KVM without a rebuild per target.
#
# NOTE: virtualbox-guest-x11 (not virtualbox-guest-utils) was tried first
# and caused a corrupted/frozen display regardless of which video
# controller (VBoxVGA/VBoxSVGA/VMSVGA) the VM used. That package ships the
# legacy Xorg vboxvideo driver, which fights with the in-kernel KMS
# vboxvideo driver Debian/Devuan kernels already ship — a well-known
# source of exactly that symptom. virtualbox-guest-utils still gives
# clipboard/seamless-mode/session integration via VBoxClient without
# forcing that legacy driver; Xorg falls back to the modern
# modesetting/KMS path instead.
virtualbox-guest-utils
open-vm-tools
open-vm-tools-desktop
qemu-guest-agent
spice-vdagent

# Desktop applications
# LibreOffice, GParted, Bluetooth (blueman), and extra media apps (ristretto,
# parole) are NOT installed here on purpose — they're multi-hundred-MB to
# install-but-rarely-used-by-everyone. They're offered as opt-in choices in
# the Calamares installer instead, so people who don't want them never
# download or boot them.
firefox-esr
mousepad
thunar-archive-plugin
file-roller
flatpak

# System utilities
sudo
curl
wget
git
htop
inxi
rsync
dosfstools
exfatprogs
ntfs-3g
fonts-noto-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji
locales
